# mm.terminal

A bounded ASCII line terminal on a caller-owned character grid. initialize
borrows a character span; its storage must outlive the Terminal. No allocations
or device initialization occur in this module. Printable ASCII occupies one
cell; other high bytes become '?'. LF starts a new line, CR returns to column
zero, BS moves left and erases, TAB inserts spaces to the next eight-column
stop, and FF clears the grid. Other controls are ignored. ANSI escape sequences
and UTF-8 decoding are not implemented.

Wrapping is deferred until the next printable character, so a full line followed
by LF advances only once. Advancing past the last row scrolls one line. A failed
initialize leaves the previous grid intact. cell returns zero outside the grid.

present redraws a caller-owned one-bit surface with mm.fonts, writes it through
mm.gfx to a one-bit or RGB565 display, and refreshes it. Supply a scratch row of
at least surface.width * 2 bytes for RGB565. The surface must fit the display and
the font must fit every cell. A failed draw or refresh preserves dirty for retry.
Callers initialize their display and schedule presentation; they may force a
redraw after display loss. The cursor position is exposed but not painted.
